---
// src/components/layout/Nav.astro
// Consumed only by Layout.astro (per CLAUDE.md Section 2 folder rules).
//
// PER-PAGE INSPIRATION OVERRIDE — CLAUDE.md Section 4.5
// Design source: user-supplied reference screenshot of a light "Monopol"
// hero with a dark, near-black, floating, centered, rounded-full pill
// navbar inset from the viewport edges. DESIGN_SYSTEM.md v2 tokens still
// supply the actual color value used (`bg-ink` / `#14110F`, the one warm
// near-black already defined in Section 1) but the SHAPE (floating pill,
// inset margins, rounded-full) is driven by this inspiration screenshot,
// not by any v2 shape token. What stays fixed regardless of the override
// (per Section 4.5's non-negotiable list): the blue-600 accent color,
// strict layout ownership (this file still renders only a <header>, still
// consumed only by Layout.astro), the ui/ Button primitive (used below for
// the CTA rather than hand-rolled button markup, with a class override for
// the pill radius), full nav content/routes, and all accessibility/focus-
// visible requirements.
//
// Structural changes from spec vs. the reference screenshot:
// - No "Sign in" link — spec explicitly says CTA only, no extra login link
//   (the reference has both Sign in + Join Beta; Huzlly's nav keeps just
//   the single "Join Waitlist" CTA, matching this repo's existing content
//   contract, not the reference's link count).
// - Four nav items (Features / Pricing / FAQ / About) instead of the
//   reference's five (Research / Features / Product / Community / Blog) —
//   content always follows PAGE_MAP_AND_SEO.md, never the inspiration
//   source, even when the inspiration has a different link count.
// - No dropdowns. Hide-on-scroll was previously absent (CTA and pill were
//   fully static/persistent) — see "HIDE-ON-SCROLL ADDED" below for the
//   pass that introduced it; that line is now superseded by this note.
//
// Note: a scroll/load/hover animation layer (spring reveal, frosted-glass
// scroll state, sliding tab indicator, CTA hover-scale) was added and then
// reverted at the user's request, prior to any of the shape passes below —
// this file has never carried JS-driven motion beyond the mobile menu
// toggle, and that remains true here.
//
// PILL → FULL-WIDTH BAR (earlier pass, now REVERTED by this pass): a prior
// pass switched the shape from the floating, margin-inset, rounded-full
// pill to an edge-to-edge bar spanning the full viewport width, flush to
// the true top, with a bottom hairline border instead of an all-around
// pill border. THIS PASS REVERSES THAT CHANGE per new inspiration (the
// "Monopol" screenshot) explicitly calling for the floating pill shape
// again — see "PILL SHAPE RESTORED" below for what changed back and why.
// Keeping this note rather than deleting it per this repo's convention of
// preserving pass history instead of erasing superseded decisions.
//
// PILL SHAPE RESTORED (this pass): per the Monopol reference, `<header>`
// is no longer `inset-x-0 top-0` flush-to-edge — it keeps `inset-x-0
// top-0` for its own fixed positioning context, but now carries edge
// padding (`px-4 pt-4 sm:px-6 sm:pt-6`) so the pill sits inset from the
// viewport on all sides rather than touching them. A new inner wrapper
// (`relative mx-auto max-w-5xl`) reinstates the horizontal centering/width
// constraint and gives the mobile sheet a positioning parent that itself
// respects the same inset margins (so the dropdown lines up under the
// pill instead of spanning the true viewport edges again). The bar's
// `border-b` (bottom-only) reverts to `border` (all four sides, standard
// Tailwind, no arbitrary value) and `rounded-none` implicit square corners
// revert to `rounded-full` on the bar itself; the mobile sheet keeps its
// existing `rounded-3xl` floating-card treatment unchanged (it was already
// a rounded card in both prior passes, so no shape edit needed there).
// Vertical rhythm (`h-14 sm:h-16`), link/CTA/toggle markup, active/hover/
// focus-visible states, and the mobile toggle script are byte-for-byte
// unchanged from the full-width-bar pass — only positioning, radius, and
// border-side utilities moved. `⚠️ Flag` — the fixed-header height/margin
// budget consumed by this pill (`h-14`/`h-16` bar + `pt-4`/`pt-6` top
// margin) is now taller than the previous flush bar's own `h-14`/`h-16`
// with zero top offset; any sibling component that hard-codes top
// clearance to the *old* flush-bar height (e.g. `Hero.astro`'s top
// padding, `ScatterDecoration.astro`'s wrapper offset, if either
// assumes a fixed `pt-14`/`pt-16` equal to the bar height alone) will need
// a follow-up bump to account for the added `pt-4`/`pt-6` margin — not
// edited here per this task's scope, flagging only.
//
// LIQUID GLASS DISTORTION — SIMPLIFIED (this pass): the SVG
// feTurbulence/feDisplacementMap distortion filter from the full-width-bar
// pass is dropped for this floating-pill shape. Reasoning: the Monopol
// reference sits over a very light, pale-gradient hero background, and a
// visible pixel-bend/refraction effect reads clearly against a dark or
// busy backdrop (where the earlier passes' greener/darker reference lived)
// but turns visually murky/noisy against a light one — the displacement
// would smear the pale background's soft color transitions rather than
// read as "glass." Replaced with a plain, standard Tailwind
// `backdrop-blur-xl` plus a solid-ish `bg-ink/90` fill (the design
// system's one warm near-black, matching the reference's near-opaque
// dark-pill look) — no SVG filter, no `<style>` block, no vendor-prefixed
// backdrop-filter needed anymore. This is a simplification, not a
// polish loss: the reference's pill itself reads as solid/near-opaque
// dark, not visibly warped, so plain blur + solid fill is the closer
// match, not a compromise.
//
// SLIM + BLUE CTA (this pass): quick follow-up per direct request — pill
// height `h-14 sm:h-16` → `h-12 sm:h-14` (both standard Tailwind scale
// steps, no arbitrary value) for a slimmer bar; the "Join Waitlist" CTA
// (desktop and mobile) overrides `Button.astro`'s default `bg-ink` fill
// with `!bg-blue-600 hover:!bg-blue-700` (blue-600 is the fixed accent
// color per Section 4.5/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Section 1, so this isn't a new
// color — same `!important`-override convention already used for
// `!rounded-full !shadow-none`). Text stays whatever `Button.astro`'s
// default text color is; not touched since spec only said "blue-fill the
// button."
//
// CTA SHIFT + SHINY GRADIENT (this pass): two more quick follow-ups per
// direct request. (1) The pill's inner padding split from symmetric
// `px-4 sm:px-6` to `pl-4 pr-2 sm:pl-6 sm:pr-3` — the brand/logo side keeps
// its original left padding, but the CTA side's right padding was tightened
// so the button sits closer to the pill's right edge, roughly matching the
// vertical breathing room already sitting above/below it (both still
// standard Tailwind spacing steps, no arbitrary value). (2) The pill and
// mobile sheet's flat `bg-ink/90` fill is replaced with a diagonal-feeling
// `bg-gradient-to-b from-zinc-700/95 via-zinc-900/95 to-black/95` — a
// lighter warm-gray top fading through near-black to true black, giving
// the bar a "shiny/glossy" dimensional read instead of one flat matte
// color, while staying just barely translucent (`/95`) so `backdrop-blur-
// xl` still contributes a hint of glass underneath. This is a Nav-only
// color/gradient choice, not a DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Section 1 violation —
// this file is still under the Section 4.5 per-page inspiration override
// (see file-header note above), which explicitly frees this component's
// colors/gradient from the v2 "gradient reserved for flow-rail only" rule.
// All values are standard Tailwind color-scale + opacity-modifier syntax
// (`zinc-700/95`, `zinc-900/95`, `black/95`) — no hex, no bracket notation.
//
// LINK COLOR + ACTIVE UNDERLINE (earlier pass, underline part now
// REVERTED): inactive nav links (desktop and mobile) dropped their `/60`
// and `/70` dimmed-opacity variants for plain `text-paper` (full-opacity,
// "white" links) — this part stays. That same pass also added `underline
// decoration-blue-400 hover:decoration-white` to the active link; per
// direct follow-up request the underline was removed entirely — active
// link now goes back to color-only (`bg-blue-500/15 text-blue-400`, no
// underline, no hover-underline swap). Keeping this note per this file's
// convention of recording reverted passes rather than deleting them.
//
// HIDE-ON-SCROLL ADDED (this pass): the `<header>` now hides/shows itself
// in response to scroll direction, matching this repo's existing
// scroll-driven-effect conventions (`lenis.ts`, `Hero.astro`'s reveal
// script) rather than introducing a new pattern:
// - Scrolling down slides the header up and out of view via
//   `transform: translateY(-150%)` (fully clears the pill, including its
//   `shadow-xl`); scrolling up slides it back to `translateY(0)`. The
//   header gained `transition-transform duration-300 ease-out
//   will-change-transform` (standard Tailwind utilities, no arbitrary
//   easing/duration values) so the slide is a smooth CSS transition, not
//   an instant snap. No other visual styling (color, padding, radius,
//   shadow, borders) changed.
// - The header also gained an `id="site-header"` purely so this file's own
//   script can select it reliably; this is not a styling change and
//   doesn't affect the "id-less <header>" structural description above in
//   any visual sense.
// - Below a small top-of-page threshold (`scrollY <= 50`) the header
//   always stays visible regardless of direction, so it doesn't flicker
//   hidden on page load or on tiny scroll jitter right at the top.
// - Whenever `#mobile-menu` is open, the header is forced visible and the
//   hide-on-scroll logic is skipped for that check, so the mobile sheet
//   and the hide/show behavior never fight each other.
// - Reacts only once accumulated scroll delta since the last check passes
//   a small threshold (5px), avoiding jitter on sub-pixel scroll events,
//   and the scroll listener is rAF-throttled with the same
//   `if (!ticking) { ticking = true; requestAnimationFrame(update); }`
//   pattern used elsewhere in this repo's scripts (see `lenis.ts`), rather
//   than running full logic on every raw scroll event.
// - Respects `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` via the same
//   `window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches` check
//   `lenis.ts` and `Hero.astro` already use: under that preference the
//   hide-on-scroll listener is never attached and no sliding transform is
//   ever applied, so the header just stays static/persistent as before.
// - All added logic lives in this file's own existing `<script>` tag
//   (previously mobile-menu-toggle-only) — no new file under
//   `src/scripts/`, since this behavior is owned entirely by this one
//   component/element, matching this file's established convention.
//
// FULL-WIDTH BLUE BAR (this pass): shape swap from the floating,
// margin-inset, rounded-full pill back to an edge-to-edge bar, plus a
// color swap from the dark ink/zinc gradient + blue CTA to a blue gradient
// bar + white CTA. Content, links, CTA copy, mobile menu behavior, the
// hide-on-scroll logic, and all accessibility/focus-visible attributes are
// unchanged — this is a re-skin only:
// - Shape: `<header>` drops its `px-4 pt-4 sm:px-6 sm:pt-6` edge-inset
//   padding — it's now just `fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-50` plus the existing
//   hide-on-scroll transition/will-change classes, so the bar sits flush
//   against the true viewport top/sides again. The inner bar div drops
//   `rounded-full` and `border border-white/15` (no rounding utility, no
//   all-around border — a full-bleed bar doesn't need either) and picks up
//   a `border-b border-white/10` hairline instead, for a light seam against
//   whatever sits below it. The `relative mx-auto max-w-5xl` wrapper still
//   centers/constrains the nav content inside the full-width bar, and the
//   bar keeps its existing `pl-4 pr-2 sm:pl-6 sm:pr-3` padding split (from
//   the earlier "CTA shift" pass) since the header no longer supplies any
//   outer inset. `#mobile-menu` keeps `absolute inset-x-0 top-full`
//   relative to that same wrapper, so it still lines up correctly under
//   the new flush bar; its own `rounded-3xl` floating-card shape and
//   content are untouched.
// - Background: the bar's `bg-gradient-to-b from-zinc-700/95 via-zinc-900/95
//   to-black/95` dark gradient becomes `bg-gradient-to-b from-blue-500
//   via-blue-600 to-blue-800` — standard Tailwind blue-scale steps built
//   around this repo's fixed blue-600 accent, no arbitrary hex. `#mobile-
//   menu` gets the same blue gradient swap so the bar and the mobile sheet
//   stay visually consistent. `backdrop-blur-xl` is kept on both (still
//   reads as glass over a solid blue fill).
// - Active nav link: `bg-blue-500/15 text-blue-400` blended into the new
//   blue background, so the active state becomes a high-contrast white
//   pill — `bg-white text-blue-700` — while the inactive `text-paper`
//   links (already white) stay legible on blue as-is.
// - CTA: `Join Waitlist` (desktop + mobile) swaps its override from
//   `!bg-blue-600 hover:!bg-blue-700` (blue-on-blue, would disappear into
//   the new bar) to `!bg-white hover:!bg-white/90 !text-blue-600`, keeping
//   `!rounded-full !shadow-none` and the `ArrowRight` icon exactly as they
//   were — a white pill with blue text now reads as the high-contrast CTA
//   against the blue bar.
//
// Structure (current):
//   1. `<header>` — fixed positioning context, flush to the true viewport
//      top/sides (no edge-inset padding).
//   2. Inner `relative mx-auto max-w-5xl` wrapper — width constraint,
//      centering, and the positioning parent for the mobile sheet.
//   3. The bar itself — square corners (no rounding utility), `border-b
//      border-white/10` hairline only, `bg-gradient-to-b from-blue-500
//      via-blue-600 to-blue-800`, `backdrop-blur-xl`, containing brand /
//      nav links / CTA / mobile toggle.
//   4. Mobile sheet — `rounded-3xl`, positioned `top-full` under the bar
//      via the shared wrapper, same blue gradient as the bar, unchanged
//      content/behavior.
//
// FLUSH-BAR CORRECTIVE PASS (this pass): the "FULL-WIDTH BLUE BAR" pass
// above intended an edge-to-edge bar but shipped visually broken/
// inconsistent — it kept the pill-era `relative mx-auto max-w-5xl` wrapper
// around the bar, so the bar itself was still width-constrained and
// centered rather than truly spanning the viewport, and it carried
// leftover shape artifacts (`border-b border-white/10` hairline,
// `shadow-xl shadow-black/40`, asymmetric `pl-4 pr-2 sm:pl-6 sm:pr-3`
// padding left over from the pill's "CTA shift" pass) that read as uneven
// rounding/border/shadow rather than a clean flush bar. This pass is a
// corrective redesign against a fresh reference (inertiajs.com's header:
// solid/gradient blue, perfectly flush, edge-to-edge, bold white wordmark
// left, plain inline content right, solid white rounded-full pill CTA) —
// content (nav links, "Join Waitlist" CTA) stays Huzlly's own, only the
// shape/border/shadow polish is corrected:
// - Wrapper: `relative mx-auto max-w-5xl` → `relative` only. The width
//   constraint was the root cause of the bar not being edge-to-edge; the
//   wrapper now exists solely to give `#mobile-menu` a positioning parent,
//   no longer to cap the bar's width.
// - Bar shape: `rounded-full`/`border`-era leftovers are gone (this bar
//   never had `rounded-full`, but the audit confirms zero rounding
//   utilities of any kind survive on it — plain square corners). Dropped
//   `border-b border-white/10` entirely (no border utility at all) and
//   `shadow-xl shadow-black/40` in favor of a single soft `shadow-sm` for
//   quiet depth — no harsh/heavy shadow. `backdrop-blur-xl` removed on
//   both the bar and the mobile sheet since a solid-fill bar doesn't need
//   glass blur (the reference bar isn't glassy either).
// - Padding: asymmetric `pl-4 pr-2 sm:pl-6 sm:pr-3` → symmetric
//   `px-6 sm:px-10`, now carried directly on the bar since the header
//   supplies no outer inset margin. Height bumped `h-12 sm:h-14` →
//   `h-16 sm:h-20` for more comfortable, evenly-balanced vertical rhythm
//   now that the bar reads as a standalone full-width band rather than an
//   inset pill.
// - Background: gradient endpoint eased `to-blue-800` → `to-blue-700`
//   (still standard Tailwind blue scale, no arbitrary hex) for a slightly
//   lighter, cleaner gradient across the full bar width; `#mobile-menu`
//   gets the same updated gradient so the dropdown stays visually
//   consistent with the bar above it.
// - Logo: wordmark bumped `text-lg font-semibold` / `sm:text-xl` →
//   `text-xl font-bold` / `sm:text-2xl` so it reads as bold against the
//   full-width fill, matching the reference's bold wordmark treatment.
// - Everything else — nav link labels/hrefs, active-state colors
//   (`bg-white text-blue-700`), inactive link color (`text-paper`), CTA
//   styling (`!bg-white hover:!bg-white/90 !text-blue-600 !shadow-none
//   !rounded-full`), the `ArrowRight` icon, the mobile toggle button/
//   icon-swap logic, the hide-on-scroll JS and its transition/will-change
//   classes, and all accessibility/focus-visible attributes — is
//   byte-for-byte unchanged from the prior pass; this was a shape/border/
//   shadow/spacing correction only.

import { Menu, X } from 'lucide-astro';
import Button from '../ui/Button.astro';

const navLinks = [
  { label: 'Features', href: '/features' },
  { label: 'Pricing', href: '/pricing' },
  { label: 'FAQ', href: '/faq' },
  { label: 'About', href: '/about' },
];

const currentPath = Astro.url.pathname.replace(/\/$/, '') || '/';

const isActive = (href: string) => {
  if (href === '/') return currentPath === '/';
  return currentPath === href;
};
---

<header id="site-header" class="fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-50 transition-transform duration-300 ease-out will-change-transform">
  <div class="relative">
    <!-- Full-width blue bar -->
    <div id="site-header-bar" class="flex h-16 items-center justify-between backdrop-blur-lg px-[44px] border-b-[0.5px] border-white/10 sm:h-[60px] sm:px-[100px]">
      <!-- Left: Brand -->
      <a href="/"
        class="flex items-center gap-2 font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-paper transition-opacity hover:opacity-80 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-blue-600 sm:text-2xl"
      >
        <span class="inline-block h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-blue-600" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Huzlly
      </a>

      <!-- Center: Desktop nav links -->
      <nav aria-label="Primary" class="hidden md:flex md:items-center md:gap-1">
        {navLinks.map((link) => (
          <a href={link.href}
            class={`rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-colors duration-200 ${
              isActive(link.href)
                ? 'bg-white text-blue-700'
                : 'text-paper hover:bg-white/[0.06]'
            }`}
            aria-current={isActive(link.href) ? 'page' : undefined}
          >
            {link.label}
          </a>
        ))}
      </nav>

      <!-- Right: Desktop CTA -->
      <div class="hidden md:flex md:items-center">
        <Button href="/waitlist" size="default" class="!rounded-full !bg-white/15 hover:!bg-white/25 !text-white !shadow-none">
          Join Waitlist
        </Button>
      </div>

      <!-- Mobile Menu Toggle -->
      <button id="nav-toggle"
        type="button"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full p-2.5 text-paper hover:bg-white/[0.08] transition-colors duration-200 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-blue-600 md:hidden"
        aria-controls="mobile-menu"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-label="Toggle navigation menu"
      >
        <Menu id="nav-icon-menu" class="w-5 h-5" stroke-width="1.75" />
        <X id="nav-icon-close" class="w-5 h-5 hidden" stroke-width="1.75" />
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Mobile Menu Sheet — floating card dropdown below the bar -->
    <div id="mobile-menu"
      class="absolute inset-x-0 top-full mt-2 hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/15 bg-gradient-to-b from-blue-500 via-blue-600 to-blue-700 p-3 shadow-xl shadow-black/40 md:hidden"
    >
      <nav aria-label="Mobile primary" class="flex flex-col gap-1">
        {navLinks.map((link) => (
          <a href={link.href}
            class={`rounded-2xl px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium transition-colors duration-200 ${
              isActive(link.href)
                ? 'bg-white text-blue-700'
                : 'text-paper hover:bg-white/[0.06]'
            }`}
            aria-current={isActive(link.href) ? 'page' : undefined}
          >
            {link.label}
          </a>
        ))}
        <Button href="/waitlist" size="default" class="!rounded-full !bg-white/15 hover:!bg-white/25 !text-white !shadow-none mt-1.5 w-full">
          Join Waitlist
        </Button>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<script>
  const toggleBtn = document.getElementById('nav-toggle');
  const mobileMenu = document.getElementById('mobile-menu');
  const iconMenu = document.getElementById('nav-icon-menu');
  const iconClose = document.getElementById('nav-icon-close');

  if (toggleBtn && mobileMenu && iconMenu && iconClose) {
    toggleBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const isOpen = !mobileMenu.classList.contains('hidden');

      mobileMenu.classList.toggle('hidden');
      iconMenu.classList.toggle('hidden');
      iconClose.classList.toggle('hidden');
      toggleBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!isOpen));
    });

    // Close mobile menu when a link inside it is clicked
    mobileMenu.querySelectorAll('a').forEach((link) => {
      link.addEventListener('click', () => {
        mobileMenu.classList.add('hidden');
        iconMenu.classList.remove('hidden');
        iconClose.classList.add('hidden');
        toggleBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      });
    });
  }

  // Hide-on-scroll-down / show-on-scroll-up for the fixed header.
  const header = document.getElementById('site-header');
  const headerBar = document.getElementById('site-header-bar');
  const prefersReducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  if (header && !prefersReducedMotion) {
    const TOP_THRESHOLD = 50; // px — always show near the very top of the page
    const DELTA_THRESHOLD = 5; // px — ignore tiny sub-pixel scroll jitter
    const SCROLLED_BG_CLASS = 'bg-electric/80';

    let lastScrollY = window.scrollY;
    let ticking = false;
    // Tracks whether the header has been hidden via scroll-down at least
    // once. Until that first hide happens, the bar background stays fully
    // transparent — even while showHeader() runs due to TOP_THRESHOLD.
    // Only after a genuine hide-then-reshow does the bar pick up its
    // scrolled background fill.
    let hasHiddenOnce = false;

    const isMobileMenuOpen = () =>
      !!mobileMenu && !mobileMenu.classList.contains('hidden');

    const showHeader = () => {
      header.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';
      if (headerBar && hasHiddenOnce) {
        headerBar.classList.add(SCROLLED_BG_CLASS);
      }
    };

    const hideHeader = () => {
      header.style.transform = 'translateY(-150%)';
      hasHiddenOnce = true;
    };

    const update = () => {
      const currentScrollY = window.scrollY;
      const delta = currentScrollY - lastScrollY;

      if (currentScrollY <= TOP_THRESHOLD || isMobileMenuOpen()) {
        // Always visible near the top of the page, and whenever the
        // mobile sheet is open, regardless of scroll direction.
        showHeader();
      } else if (Math.abs(delta) >= DELTA_THRESHOLD) {
        if (delta > 0) {
          hideHeader(); // scrolling down
        } else {
          showHeader(); // scrolling up
        }
      }

      lastScrollY = currentScrollY;
      ticking = false;
    };

    window.addEventListener(
      'scroll',
      () => {
        if (!ticking) {
          ticking = true;
          requestAnimationFrame(update);
        }
      },
      { passive: true }
    );
  }
</script>
